Add faster Keccak-p[1600]x4 backends for aarch64

Off x86-64, Keccak-p[1600]x4 used fallback-on1, i.e., four serial plain 64-bit permutations, which
is about a quarter of the time of VOLEitH proving and verification on Apple M4. Use the AArch64
code that the pinned XKCP revision already has instead:

* With the ARMv8.4-A SHA3 instructions (e.g., Apple M1 and later), a new fallback-on2 backend
  that runs two KeccakP-1600-times2/ARMv8A (NEON+SHA3) permutations. On an M4 this is ~2.1x
  faster than four serial permutations, and ~1.4x faster than the hybrid x4 core.
* Otherwise, the scalar+NEON hybrid x4 core from KeccakP-1600-times4/ARMv8A (~1.5x faster than
  four serial permutations; the pure-NEON x2 code is slower than serial without SHA3).

The assembly uses the C preprocessor, which GCC (unlike Clang) does not apply to .s files, so
build it with -x assembler-with-cpp.

TODO(cjpatton) Propose fallback-on2 and the meson.build change to the XKCP and faest-arch-opt
